Kernel -Linus Torvalds in 1991.  -Its the core working component of OS.
The kernel is the core code of an OS that acts as a bridge between your computer's hardware (CPU, memory, storage) and the software applications you run. It was created in 1991 by a student named Linus Torvalds. 

The Operating System (Linux Distributions): A kernel alone can't do much for an everyday user. To make it a usable operating system, developers bundle the Linux kernel with standard system utilities, graphical interfaces, web browsers, and package managers. These complete packages are called Linux Distributions (or "Distros"). 
